WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.130
<b>Hakuo 
Academy</b>

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:08.760
Hello. I'm the Sanzenin 
family's maid, Maria.

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:10.150
<b>Maria</b>

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:14.490
On the job, I tend to be 
seen as an older woman,

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.120
but I'm still just seventee—

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.250
You've grown so 
big, Little President!

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.260
Hey, do you have a boyfriend yet?

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.400
Wh— Makimura-sensei, what are you...

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:28.570
Oh, that would be my boyfriend.

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:32.550
Fall for me and you'll get burned!

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:37.550
<i>That's quite a 
reliable-looking boyfriend...</i>

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:40.000
Sorry! We'll talk later!

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.450
Let us go, my honey.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.030
A boyfriend, eh?

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.320
Huh... Huh?

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.520
I can't hear anything...

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:25.410
Oh, that's quite the antique.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:27.900
Would you like me to fix it?

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:31.380
I just happen to have 
a broken one, too.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:35.630
Hm? But, if it's broken, 
what's the point?

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:37.470
No need to worry.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.480
Even if they're both broken,

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.760
as long as it's different 
parts that don't work...

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:44.770
They can be combined 
into a working one.

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:46.820
Like this.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:49.480
Whoa!

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:53.060
Not bad! You really are a genius!

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.600
They don't call you a 
Hakuo Old Boy for nothing.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:57.230
You're welcome.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:03.410
But I was never at the top 
of my class in this school.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:04.700
What? Really?

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:07.660
Yes. There was a genius...

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:11.290
A real genius, in the same grade as me.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.920
Little President! 
There's been an incident!

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:18.980
Wait, what are you reading?

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:21.760
Oh, this?

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:24.990
It's <i>Sunday</i>... in Polynesian.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:29.100
<i>I'm not sure if that's an 
impressive book or not...</i>

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:32.990
So, Vice President Makimura-san,
 what's this incident?

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:35.840
Oh! That's right!
 It's terrible, Little President!

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:37.550
Look outside!

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:38.690
Outside?

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:43.120
I hadn't even noticed!

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:46.580
It's cold and snow is falling!
 What should we do?

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:50.830
Let's set up the heated table, then.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:54.330
That's my Little President! 
What an ingenious solution!

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:00.770
So warm...

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:03.840
You really are amazing 
though, Little President.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:08.710
Skipping grades to start 
high school at age 10,

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:11.550
superior at both academics and sports,

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:15.850
and becoming student council 
president as a first year.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.070
And so cute to top it all off!

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:22.160
It's absolutely criminal, 
Little President!

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:26.700
Please, stop calling me 
Little President already.

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:30.870
I have a name, you know. It's Maria.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:36.420
By the way, Makimura-san, 
I hear you started a new club.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:39.840
The Video Research Club, 
or something like that?

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:44.240
Yeah! I thought I'd make 
a record of your growth.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:47.950
I mean, all the guys love you, 
so there's an obvious demand.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:52.890
If you meet that demand, this 
school would be full of criminals...

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:56.020
But I've already shot quite a few.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:57.750
What?

00:04:56.930 --> 00:04:57.750
Look.

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:18.960
I'm sorry. My hand slipped.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:22.710
Oh... Your hand slipped, eh?

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:26.000
Anyway, you can't show videos!

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.550
Aw, fine then...

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:31.350
I'll start with just sound.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:33.160
I guess that's...

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:37.540
Oh, Experimental Caregiver 
Robot Number 1-kun...

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:39.690
Excuse me, Makimura-san.

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:42.570
The teacher says it's time to meet.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:46.030
Oh, no! I have to declare my thesis!

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.470
I'll see you later!

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:49.070
Right, right.

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:50.680
Hurry!

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:10.310
This is Maria. Um, um...

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:12.720
I'm the student council president.

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:23.130
This is Maria. Um, um...

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:25.520
I'm the student council presiden—

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:34.850
Uh, okay, I will now sing 
a song about "Maria."

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.850
The M of Maria is for Ma—

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:40.450
I almost forgot, Maria...

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:46.070
I'm sorry. My hand slipped.

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:49.280
O-Okay, just be careful...

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:51.680
By the way,

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:53.480
what's on this tape?

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:56.520
No idea. The player's been
 broken all this time...

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.320
Really? Sounds interesting!

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:00.690
Let's listen and see what's—

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:03.150
You mustn't listen to it.

00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:05.850
Whoa! Maria-san, why are you here?!

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:10.530
I suddenly remembered that I left 
something here at this school.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.460
Wait, so that tape's yours?

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:16.010
That's gotta be interesting!
 Let us hear it!

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:18.910
Sure, I don't mind...

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:21.920
But my hand may slip.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:25.790
Uh... Never mind, then.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:32.520
That was lucky. 
I remembered just in time.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:42.980
<b>Sanzenin</b>

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:42.980
We certainly got lots 
of mail again today.

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:47.690
Pizza, sushi, and even a 
"maid delivery service"...

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:52.990
This one looks quite a 
bit like a love letter...

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:54.730
To Hayate Ayasaki-kun

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:56.030
It's for Hayate-kun. What could it be?

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:01.620
<i>Could this be a real love letter?!</i>

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:04.130
<i>It can't be, can it?</i>

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:08.260
<i>But there's a return address... and...</i>

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:13.510
<i>It has the smell of a cute girl...</i>

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:16.600
Huh? A love letter for me?

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:23.560
So... how should I turn 
this one down, Maria-san?

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:26.980
You make your decision two 
seconds after receiving it?

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:29.410
But, you're turning her 
down, just like that?

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:32.900
What about going to meet her once,

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:36.610
and dating her if she's cute?

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:39.450
Don't you ever think about that?

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:42.970
Do I look that clever to you?

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:45.710
Sorry. I guess you don't.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:49.450
But, really, how should 
I turn her down?

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:52.970
You seem like you must 
receive a lot of these.

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:57.850
Well, I did receive them all 
the time in high school...

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:02.570
But, well... they gave me 
a sort of criminal vibe...

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:05.980
I see.

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:09.560
Well, at any rate, I'd better read it.

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:11.610
<b>I love you I love you I love you I love you</b>

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:15.700
Uh... I'm not really into 
girls who love obsessively...

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:19.870
Hayate-kun... there's no 
guarantee on the "love" part.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:23.190
W-Well, anyway, it 
has a return address.

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:26.830
I should send a letter 
of refusal there, right?

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:31.380
R-Right. As gently as you possibly can.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.580
Are you sure about that?

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:35.880
Miss Nagi!

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:40.260
You two don't understand how 
to conquer obsessive lovers!

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:42.980
Er, it's not like I want to conquer—

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:45.640
There's a different anime about that.

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:48.270
Write it... like this!

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:49.650
I don't know who said anything 
about love or hate, but<b><i> no thanks!</i></b>

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:50.940
Send!

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:53.510
Preparation complete!

00:09:53.090 --> 00:09:54.680
<b>Preparation complete</b>

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:59.740
That girl's 12,000 years too early 
to lay a hand on my Hayate.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:03.740
<b>Sanzenin</b>

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:08.110
<i>That was fast!</i>

00:10:08.110 --> 00:10:10.210
<i>Is this the power of obsessive love?!</i>

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:14.840
<b>I'll kill you I'll kill you I'll kill you I'll kill you</b>

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:14.270
And I think she's 
raised the bar a bit...

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:16.970
What should we do, Miss Nagi?!

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:20.260
We have no choice. 
If that's how it is...

00:10:20.740 --> 00:10:23.470
We'll have to take the classic 
romantic comedy route!

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:25.590
<i>Classic...</i>

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:27.080
<i>...romantic comedy route?</i>

00:10:32.530 --> 00:10:34.450
Sure is a peaceful day.

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:37.790
Feels a little lacking in 
stimulation, though...

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.410
<b>Romantic Comedy Fair</b>

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.410
<b>Definitive Edition
 Rom-Com</b>

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.410
<b>The Gold Standard
 of Rom-Com</b>

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.410
<b>Staff's 
Pick!</b>

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:45.570
<i>That's right! In a classic romantic 
comedy, right about now...</i>

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:48.090
<i>Nishizawa-san!</i>

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:50.950
<i>Hayate-kun!</i>

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:53.130
<i>He looks awesome as always.</i>

00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:56.460
<i>So, how about a date?</i>

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:58.400
<i>I-I'd love to!</i>

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:04.830
No, no, no. That's not 
a romantic comedy.

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:07.210
Let's see... The punch line would be...

00:11:07.210 --> 00:11:08.800
Hayate-kun!

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:13.190
Maria-san!

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:17.250
You look lovely as usual today.

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:22.530
Seriously?!

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:25.280
<b>Commercial Connecting Theater</b>

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:25.280
I hope I grow up soon...

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:27.550
I know this is sudden,

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:32.570
<b>Celebrating 10 Episodes  
Character Popularity Contest</b>

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:32.980
but in celebration of the 10th episode, 
it's a Character Popularity Contest!

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:34.400
The winner gets to...

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:35.790
...strip!

00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:38.730
Why did you do that?

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:41.230
I thought it would liven things up.

00:11:41.230 --> 00:11:43.810
Was that all you could 
think of to liven things up?

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:47.120
B-But I thought it would be fun...

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:48.910
How is that fun?

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:50.060
W-Well...

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:52.730
So, we can call it off, yes?

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:53.480
Yes.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:56.900
<b>Commercial Connecting Theater</b>

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:56.900
I'm still only seventeen!

00:11:56.900 --> 00:12:00.470
Maria-san seems like she'd 
use some special technique.

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:01.650
Yeah...

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:03.640
You know, I think...

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:07.780
that broom she's always holding 
actually conceals a sword,

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:11.400
and she goes around saying things like, 
"Once again, I have cut a worthless object."

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:13.670
No way. I say she transforms.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:16.110
Every night, she turns 
into a pretty soldier in a mini-skirt

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:18.300
and punishes people in 
the name of the moon.

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:19.980
I can picture that!

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:23.430
Right? Ignoring the 
"pretty" part, at least...

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:30.650
What? Maria-san and I go on a 
date and act like we're in love?

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:34.640
Indeed. The girl will most 
likely be watching you,

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:36.840
so if she sees you acting 
like a silly couple,

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:38.920
she'll give up and go away!

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:40.610
A-Are you sure?

00:12:40.970 --> 00:12:43.530
Yes. When dealing with 
an obsessive lover,

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:47.630
if you remove all flags early, 
it won't grow into a problem.

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:49.080
So, with that...

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:53.870
<b>Operation: Lovey-Dovey Fake Date
 </b>by Nagi 
 Starring: Hayate Ayasaki, Maria<b></b>

00:12:49.650 --> 00:12:53.870
Eliminate Obsessive Lovers! 
Operation: Heart-Pounding Date!

00:12:55.110 --> 00:12:57.940
And don't you get any weird ideas.

00:12:57.940 --> 00:12:59.920
Y-Yes, sir...

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:05.730
So, as Miss Nagi ordered, 
our fake date has begun...

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:09.430
Shall we start by shopping
 for clothes, as she directed?

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:14.350
Don't get the wrong idea!

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:16.920
It was written in Miss Nagi's scenario!

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:19.350
Yes, I know!

00:13:19.350 --> 00:13:21.860
I wasn't flustered or anything, 
so what's the problem?

00:13:22.430 --> 00:13:25.290
But do you really think 
that girl will give up?

00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:28.080
I just hope it doesn't make
 her even more angry.

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:31.660
<i>Damn! What's with that guy?!</i>

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:35.620
<i>Holding hands with a 
cute maid like her!</i>

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:38.630
<i>But, now that I think about it,</i>

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:41.530
<i>this is the first time I've held 
hands with a boy like this.</i>

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:46.740
<i>So my first time was with Hayate-kun...</i>

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:49.840
Um, is something wrong?

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:52.720
Huh? N-No, nothing.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:55.730
I was just wondering if 
the plan is working...

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:59.860
I wonder what they're talking about...

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:03.410
This really is a big help, though.

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:07.820
We don't know anything 
about dates, after all, do we?

00:14:09.460 --> 00:14:13.950
Hayate-kun, don't forget, 
I <i>am</i> older than you.

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:15.910
Huh? Oh... Right...

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:21.340
So you should treat me more 
like... well, an older lady.

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:23.720
O-Okay, I understand.

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:27.880
For now, let's just 
follow this scenario.

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:29.760
I see...

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:33.510
So, the two of them are out 
on a fake date right now?

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:38.990
Yeah. My "king of absolute obedience 
scenario" is the perfect plan.

00:14:38.990 --> 00:14:42.660
Any obsessive lover who sees it 
will be defeated in a heartbeat.

00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:44.780
You're amazing, Nagi.

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:50.290
But, you don't think it would actually
 fuel this obsessive girl's rage?

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:51.210
Huh?

00:14:52.180 --> 00:14:54.030
Fuel her rage, eh?

00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:59.600
Was that true?

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:03.070
Damn that punk! He'll pay for this!

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:06.190
Using the letter I wrote as 
a prank because I was bored

00:15:06.190 --> 00:15:08.560
to go on a date with that maid?!

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:11.140
<i>Father, what's that letter?</i>

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:12.300
<i>Nothing.</i>

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:16.720
<i>But you certainly have the 
sweet smell of a young girl...</i>

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:20.020
I won't let him!

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:23.630
What? It was him?

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:27.360
Yes... So that's what he used 
the stationery I gave him for...

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:32.110
Oh, Hayate-kun! This outfit is so cute!

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:35.060
Yes. I'm sure it'll look great on you.

00:15:34.310 --> 00:15:36.200
Go try it on, Hayate-kun!

00:15:37.050 --> 00:15:38.200
Why me?

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:40.970
Well, why not?

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:43.790
We're here shopping together, after all.

00:15:43.990 --> 00:15:46.300
That logic makes no sense!

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:50.500
Okay, I'll add it to the scenario.

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:54.300
"Hayate-kun buys a girl's outfit, 
and something stirs in him."

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:57.060
Don't make weird things stir in me!

00:15:57.430 --> 00:16:00.990
Oh, look, I didn't 
even have to write it.

00:16:00.990 --> 00:16:04.390
It already says, "Maria joyfully 
dresses Hayate as a girl."

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:06.690
<i>Miss Nagi...</i>

00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:11.780
I lost them...

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:13.740
But...

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:16.150
I must have been imagining it.

00:16:16.150 --> 00:16:17.990
Those two would never...

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:23.340
Wow! The mini-skirt looks 
great on you, too!

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:24.500
Seriously...

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.770
This isn't right, Maria-san!

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:28.500
<i>Crash...</i>

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:32.880
Gosh, dates are fun, 
aren't they, Hayate-kun?

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:35.790
I feel as though I've lost something.

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:37.300
Oh, please.

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:40.470
I was only following the scenario.

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:43.390
So was I just imagining 
that wild enthusiasm?

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:47.560
So, what happens next?

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:49.000
Let's see...

00:16:52.550 --> 00:16:53.470
What's wrong?

00:16:53.470 --> 00:16:55.450
I-It's... just...

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:58.190
Really, what is it, Hayate-kun?

00:16:58.190 --> 00:17:00.480
If you don't follow the scenario,

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:02.750
you'll make that obsessive 
something-or-other angry.

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:04.970
Yeah, but this...

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:08.420
Don't argue. Do as the scenario says—

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:10.340
<b>Chapter 3: Maria Strips!!  
(Trying on a swimsuit)</b>  
(Even though she'll probably look ugly.)

00:17:22.570 --> 00:17:25.060
D-Don't, Hayate-kun!

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:26.930
That voice...

00:17:26.930 --> 00:17:28.560
Not yet!

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:32.580
I said, don't look at me yet!

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:34.190
I-I know!

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:37.770
<i>Crash...</i>

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:40.130
Hina-san, over here!

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:41.090
Ayumu?

00:17:41.090 --> 00:17:43.290
A-Are those two...

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:48.720
Anyway, we have to follow them!

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:50.310
R-Roger!

00:17:54.990 --> 00:17:56.590
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:02.390
What do you think?

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:06.060
I changed into the clothes we 
bought, like the scenario said.

00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:09.770
Wow! It looks great on you, Maria-san!

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:11.510
So, what's next?

00:18:11.510 --> 00:18:12.400
Let's see...

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:14.320
<b>Final Chapter  
Now that the shopping is finished, to the aquarium we GO!!  
</b>(Settle everything there!!)

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:18.980
<b>Nogata Aquarium</b>

00:18:23.340 --> 00:18:26.980
Wow! Hayate-kun, they're 
doing a dolphin show!

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:28.330
It looks that way.

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:31.960
Since we're here, let's watch 
from the front, Hayate-kun!

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:34.380
Maria-san! Watch out!

00:18:41.420 --> 00:18:43.720
See? If you get too close,

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:46.020
the clothes you just 
bought will get wet.

00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:49.030
Th-Thank you...

00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:54.900
I-I'm sorry!

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:56.780
Oh, no, I'm sorry I was so...

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:59.690
Th-The dolphins are cute, aren't they?

00:18:59.690 --> 00:19:01.780
Y-Yes, they are.

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:06.970
<i>That wasn't good. I can't believe
 I got flustered over that.</i>

00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:13.270
<i>As an older lady, I need 
to show some dignity.</i>

00:19:13.640 --> 00:19:15.130
Hayate-kun!

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:16.260
Y-Yes?

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:22.010
I-It's not as if I have 
feelings for you or anything!

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:24.760
Huh? Oh... Okay.

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:28.010
<i>This is very bad!</i>

00:19:28.010 --> 00:19:30.890
<i>I somehow feel like I've just 
suffered a crushing defeat!</i>

00:19:31.990 --> 00:19:33.640
<i>Darn you, Hayate-kun!</i>

00:19:33.640 --> 00:19:37.400
<i>Now I'm going to show 
you how mature I can be!</i>

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:41.720
<i>That damn butler...</i>

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:44.200
<i>Going out on a date at his age!</i>

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:48.000
<i>But I will not just 
stand by in silence!</i>

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:51.580
<i>If I leap into her arms 
in this cute body...</i>

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:56.690
<i>A kind maid like her will have 
no choice but to embrace me!</i>

00:19:57.850 --> 00:20:01.290
Oh, Hayate-kun! Look 
at the cute penguins!

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:03.430
<i>She's here!</i>

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:09.520
<i>All right, Miss Maid, now is the 
time for you to kindly embrace me!</i>

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:20.030
Wow! This cute penguin jumped 
right into my arms, Maria-san!

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.820
<i>No! I wanted the maid to...</i>

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:29.250
Getting all excited over a penguin...

00:20:29.250 --> 00:20:31.370
You're such a child, Hayate-kun.

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:35.190
Uh, but...

00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:36.500
<i>I win!</i>

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:39.530
Well, let's move on, Hayate-kun.

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:50.000
But, Maria-san, do you 
really think the sender

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:51.350
of that letter will give up now?

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:53.360
I'm not sure.

00:20:53.360 --> 00:20:56.300
I've had fun today, though.

00:20:56.300 --> 00:20:58.320
It feels sort of like a real date.

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:00.460
Has it been fun for you?

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:03.130
Oh... Yes...

00:21:12.270 --> 00:21:15.370
Yes. I've had fun, too.

00:21:19.570 --> 00:21:22.840
Welcome to Nogata Aquarium.

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:24.490
Hey! Hina-san!

00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:25.820
This is the sardine area.

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:27.590
Sorry! I really wanted 
to push the button...

00:21:27.920 --> 00:21:29.680
Oh... Hinagiku-san and...

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:31.850
Nishizawa-san? Why are you...

00:21:33.950 --> 00:21:36.270
<i>Is this my chance?</i>

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:38.480
<i>I should take advantage of this...</i>

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:41.830
Wh-What are <i>you</i> doing here?!

00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:44.070
Are you two going out or something?!

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:45.150
What?!

00:21:46.050 --> 00:21:48.070
Of course not!

00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:51.580
Yeah, what she said! This 
is just blah-blah-blah...

00:21:54.940 --> 00:21:55.540
Wh—

00:21:55.610 --> 00:21:57.050
Oh, that's all?

00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:59.060
Of course!

00:21:59.060 --> 00:22:03.370
Well, we haven't seen the dolphin 
show yet, so we'll be going.

00:22:03.370 --> 00:22:05.220
Oh, okay. It was good to see you.

00:22:13.900 --> 00:22:16.760
I guess we really did 
look like boyfriend and girlfriend.

00:22:17.360 --> 00:22:20.390
Nothing less from a plan 
designed by Miss Nagi!

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:23.730
<i>A boyfriend, huh?</i>

00:22:24.520 --> 00:22:27.830
<i>Someday, I hope I'll 
find someone like that,</i>

00:22:27.830 --> 00:22:29.510
<i>and we can be together like this...</i>

00:22:30.320 --> 00:22:33.360
Um, is something wrong, Maria-san?

00:22:33.360 --> 00:22:36.410
What? N-No, nothing!

00:22:36.780 --> 00:22:39.600
You really lack delicacy, Hayate-kun!

00:22:39.600 --> 00:22:42.900
Huh? Hey! Maria-san!

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:22.320
<b>Next Time</b>
